  "query_preview": "..\n(Thursday through Monday)\nIssued at 131 PM CDT Tue Jul 21 2026\n\nAn expansive upper-level ridge will dominate the region, sustaining \nhot and primarily dry conditions throughout the forecast period. By \nFriday, the ridge axis will shift briefly toward the Four Corners, \nallowing weak northerly flow aloft to potentially steer mountain-\ninitiated convection from New Mexico into the northwestern portion \nof the area. Otherwise, dry conditions will persist for the next \nseven days.\n\nWidespread triple-digit temperatures are expected, with most areas \nreaching 100-105F throughout the week and into the weekend. Extreme \nheat, with peak temperatures of 110-115F, will be concentrated \nacross the Big Bend and Rio Grande Valley during this time.",
